#include \(dqserver.h\(dq

int server_socket_create(const char *path, int no_peercred);
.EE
.SH DESCRIPTION
Creates an \f[CR]AF_UNIX\f[R] stream socket, binds it to the filesystem
\f[CR]path\f[R], and begins listening for connections.
.PP
The function performs the following steps:
.IP "1." 3
Validates that \f[CR]path\f[R] fits within \f[CR]sun_path\f[R]
(typically 108 bytes).
.IP "2." 3
Creates a \f[CR]SOCK_STREAM\f[R] socket in the \f[CR]AF_UNIX\f[R]
domain.
.IP "3." 3
Sets \f[CR]SO_REUSEADDR\f[R] on the socket.
.IP "4." 3
On Cygwin, if \f[CR]no_peercred\f[R] is set, calls
\f[CR]setsockopt(fd, SOL_SOCKET, SO_PEERCRED, NULL, 0)\f[R] to disable
the credential handshake (see NOTES).
.IP "5." 3
Removes any existing socket file at \f[CR]path\f[R] via
\f[CR]unlink()\f[R].
.IP "6." 3
Binds the socket to \f[CR]path\f[R].
.IP "7." 3
Sets the socket file permissions to \f[CR]0600\f[R] (owner read/write
only).
.IP "8." 3
Calls \f[CR]listen()\f[R] with \f[CR]SOMAXCONN\f[R] backlog.
.SH PARAMETERS
.IP \(bu 2
\f[B]path\f[R] \(en Filesystem path for the Unix domain socket.
Must be shorter than \f[CR]sizeof(struct sockaddr_un.sun_path)\f[R]
(typically 108 bytes).
The parent directory must already exist; use the server\(cqs
\f[CR]resolve_socket_path()\f[R] to create it if needed.
.IP \(bu 2
\f[B]no_peercred\f[R] \(en If non\-zero, disables the Cygwin
\f[CR]SO_PEERCRED\f[R] credential handshake.
This flag has no effect on non\-Cygwin platforms.
Set to \f[CR]1\f[R] when Python or other non\-C clients will connect
(see NOTES).
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns the listening socket file descriptor on success (a non\-negative
integer).
.PP
Returns \f[CR]\-1\f[R] on error, with \f[CR]errno\f[R] set
appropriately.
